      "href": "readings/blieszner-2014/full.html",
      "text": "The emergence of multiple forms of social media, where people can become acquainted with many others via the Internet, changes the definition of friend for some people and expands the range of possible contacts (Huberman, Romero, and Wu, 2008), some of whom may become friends.\n\nUnique Features of Friend Ties\n\nMany family relationships belong to certain segments of the lifespan and depend upon the actions of others. Prepubescent children cannot be parents, intergenerational bonds are contingent upon availability of younger and older family members, and becoming a grandparent occurs not when one chooses, but when one's offspring bear children. In later years, retirement and outliving a child or spouse remove employee and parent or marital roles, respectively. But friendship is a close relationship that begins early and can endure throughout life.",
