      "pageLabel": "원문 읽기",
      "href": "readings/park-mcdonough-2013/full.html",
      "text": "Advanced age is accompanied by deterioration of cognitive processes. However, brain function does not passively decline with age, as most cognitive aging theories would have predicted, but rather the aging brain retains plasticity and adapts to these challenges by recruiting additional neural resources and/or reorganizing neural networks to best utilize the available neural circuitry (Davis et al., 2008; Park & Reuter-Lorenz, 2009).",
      "searchText": "the dynamic aging mind: revelations from functional neuroimaging research 원문 읽기 advanced age is accompanied by deterioration of cognitive processes. however, brain function does not passively decline with age, as most cognitive aging theories would have predicted, but rather the aging brain retains plasticity and adapts to these challenges by recruiting additional neural resources and/or reorganizing neural networks to best utilize the available neural circuitry (davis et al., 2008; park & reuter-lorenz, 2009).",
